Step 3 — Allow internal network → anywhere
sudo iptables -A FORWARD -i br-c39f0aea5210 -o br-288a365a777c -j ACCEPT

This allows:

192.168.60.0 → 10.9.0.0
Step 4 — Allow return traffic (stateful rule)
sudo iptables -A FORWARD -m state --state ESTABLISHED,RELATED -j ACCEPT

This allows replies.

Step 5 — Test the firewall

Enter HostA container:

sudo docker exec -it hostA-10.9.0.5 bash

Try pinging internal hosts:

ping 192.168.60.5

It should FAIL (blocked).

Step 6 — Test internal → external

Enter Host1:

sudo docker exec -it host1-192.168.60.5 bash

Then:

ping 10.9.0.5

This should WORK.

Step 7 — Show firewall rules (for lab screenshot)

Run:

sudo iptables -L -v

Take screenshot for your lab report.
